Downloaded at run time, not redistributed
=========================================

MakerMods Metal arm
  https://github.com/makermods-robotics/metal-python-ros, commit ef4181f1305cbcfc63431d3bcfb96f5fb7f72763 (metal_sdk/example/urdf/metal_with_gripper.urdf)
  The repository has no license file. Its ROS package manifests give the license as "Business", and its metal_sdk/ folder, which holds this URDF, has an MIT license (Copyright (c) 2025 MakerMods). MakerMods has not confirmed which terms apply to the URDF.
  The first use of the Metal arm's profile downloads the URDF into <cache>/real/ on the user's machine; every load checks its SHA-256 and converts it into the kinematic chain (joint origins, axes and limits) in memory (src/robouse/real/kinematics.py). Neither the URDF nor the chain is in the repository or the package; robouse 0.2.0 to 0.5.0 shipped the chain as robouse/real/data/metal_chain.json.

robouse fetch-assets and the suites download these at pinned revisions, with SHA-256 checks, under their own licenses: MuJoCo Menagerie robot models (BSD-3-Clause, Apache-2.0 or MIT, each with its LICENSE), RoboCasa assets (CC BY 4.0), the HumanoidBench H1 walking policy (unitree_rl_gym, BSD-3-Clause), and Meta-World's scripted policies (MIT), which `robouse export` copies into exported reference solutions together with Meta-World's license.

